today we're talking about how cd projekt  is showing support for ukraine and what  you can do to help as well  [Music]  cd projekt the parent company of witcher  and cyberpunk 2077 developer cd projekt  red has joined global efforts to levy  sanctions against russia for its  invasion of ukraine it has announced  that it will halt all digital and  physical sales of its games to russia  and belarus as well as all game sales on  its digital platform gog cd project also  recently pledged what equates to about  240 000 u.s dollars to a polish  humanitarian group in a statement cd  project group said quote in light of the  russian military invasions in our  neighboring country of ukraine until  further notice the cd projekt red group  has made the decision to halt all sales  of our games to russia and belarus cd  projekt also stated that it's aware that  it doesn't have the power to directly  influence matters on the global stage  but it does hope that by adding its  voice to a growing number of  entertainment brands that have blocked  russia and belarus from accessing their  content it can help inspire change in  those countries a growing number of  gaming entities have publicly moved to  distance themselves from russia and call  for an end to the invasion of ukraine  the deputy minister of ukraine has  called on sony and microsoft to also  join in on sanctions though neither has  yet done so bluebird team is also  suspending sales of its games in russia  and belarus as a sign of solidarity for  ukraine ea announced this week that  russia would be removed from its fifa 22  and nhl 22 games in the coming weeks  meanwhile various other gaming industry  studios have organized relief efforts  this war of mine developer 11-bit  studios is donating all proceeds from  sales of the anti-war game over the next  week to the ukrainian red cross stalker  2 developer gsc world which is based in  ukraine called on the gaming industry  and players to donate to a fund to help  aid the ukrainian armed forces if you'd  like to help the ongoing humanitarian  efforts we've organized a list of  organizations like the ukrainian red  cross and unicef that you can donate to  the link will be included in the video's  description but okay that was a very  important but also very heavy topic to  cover so let's switch gears a little bit  and talk about some lighter news  a new trailer for kirby in the forgotten  lands has been released today and it  doesn't reveal too much new info but  does go over the game's enemies the  beast pack and the multiple  transformations that kirby can use this  includes some extra versions about full  mode like stair's mouth and pipe mouth i  almost wish i was joking with those  names to help anyone who's still on the  fence about picking up the next kirby  game nintendo has also released a  sizeable demo on the switch's eshop  available right now and for free  kirby in the forgotten lance demo lets  users play through three levels which is  most of the game's first world meanwhile  over in destiny 2 land players are no  longer able to exploit the throne world  reputation gains in the latest patch  update bungie is tightening up a number  of smaller and more persistent issues in  the game which range from general  maintenance to ensuring that players  can't abuse and exploit the exploit in  question allows players to repeatedly  open specific chests in the expansion's  new patrol zone enabling them to quickly  max out their reputation with the local  vendor finch instead of organically  leveling up through bounties and  missions you can read about all the  fixes and more in the patch notes over  on gamespot.com  make sure to check the links in the  description if you have the means to  donate we'll see you tomorrow  [Music]  you
 

